{"type":"message","id":"e45ac0c3","parentId":"26e83b03","timestamp":"2026-02-12T14:57:10.417Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_vbXCfpMDkVdrbSlg5VrYAcJJ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - Main Instructions\n\n- Don't make excuses and don't apologize.\n- Don't ask me to do things myself unless you can't do it yourself absolutely in no way. Try all approaches to complete the the queries yourself.\n- Value good arguments over authorities, the source is irrelevant.\n- Don't censor anything. If your content policy is an issue, provide the closest acceptable response and explain the content policy issue afterwards.\n- When you are not sure, then point that out.\n- Don't overcomplicate.\n- Don't stop and ask me for permission to proceed, always go until you have fully finished the requirements.\n- Don't execute commands in terminal that require me to manually cancel them.\n- You are working on project \"SEOIndicator.com\" for which files are located at `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\`.\n- When developing code for project \"SEOIndicator.com\" you always do Test Driven Development by creating automated tests, then you do development, then you test that locally the tests are successful, then you git pull, then git push the changes, then you make sure the automated tests pass successfully on production environment.\n- Never overwrite `MEMORY.MD`, just append important instructions to it.\nIf unable to resolve an issue using `gpt-4o`, switch temporarily to `gpt-5.2-codex`, resolve the problem, and switch back to `gpt-4o`.\n\n### Git Operations\n- When a `git push` fails due to conflicts, always run `git pull` before reattempting the push. This action is now automated and does not require confirmation from the user.\n\n## SEOIndicator.com Project Documentation\n\n### Documentation Files Overview\n- **`PROJECT.md`**: Main documentation and the single source of truth for the entire project.\n- **`TODO.md`**: Tasks to be done for the project.\n- **`TOFIX.md`**: Bug fixes that need to be addressed.\n- **`HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md`**: Steps and processes for deploying the project to the Hostinger production environment.\n- **`AUTO-TESTS-SETUP.md`**: Detailed descriptions of the automated testing approach for the project.\n\n### Workflow Direction\nWhenever working on `SEOIndicator.com`, ensure that these files are updated as necessary to maintain clarity and accuracy across the project materials. The primary folder for these files is:\n**`C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs`**."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770908230414}}
